STRINGBUFFER Class

StringBuffer - StringBuffer class is very similar to String class but the object created using StringBuffer class are mutable & Thread-Safe.
StringBuffer doesn't use the concept of String Constant Pool, all the objects will be created in Heap Area.

StringBuffer (Mutable & Thread-Safe)
a. Defined in java.lang.StringBuffer
b. Mutable (can be changed without creating a new object)
c. d. Thread-safe (synchronized methods)
Better performance than String for frequent modifications

Example:
StringBuffer sb = new StringBuffer("Hello");
sb.append(" World");  // Modifies existing object
System.out.println(sb);  // Output: Hello World

Methods of StringBuffer
1. append(value) - returntype is StringBuffer
This method is used to append (concatenate) the  values.

2. insert(index, value) - returntype is StringBuffer
This method is used to insert given value in the string at the specified index.

3. delete(int start, int end) - returntype is StringBuffer
This method is used to delete the characters present in the specified range.

4. deleteCharAt(int index) - returntype is StringBuffer
This method is used to remove the character given at the specified index.

5. replace(int start, int end, StringBuffer) - returntype is StringBuffer
This method is used to replace the set of characters from the given range with new value.

6. reverse() - returntype of is StringBuffer
This is used to reverse the string in the same object.

7. toString() - returntype is String
This is used to return the data of the stringbuffer in string format.